  "summary": "New preprints pair deep sequence models with ancestry-, drug- and tissue-resolved eQTL maps to link noncoding risk variants to effector genes and cell states.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is resolving how noncoding variation acts across cellular contexts. On the predictive side, AlphaGenome 2 models cell-type-specific regulatory activity and variant effects from 1-Mb sequence across cell states. ChromBPNet models of 17 hematopoietic cell types score 302,830 variants and show lineage-structured predicted accessibility effects. Empirical context-specific QTL work extends this. Drug-response eQTLs for ALK inhibition were mapped in single-cell RNA-seq of iPSC-derived multi-cell cultures from 49 donors. West African ancestry associates with greater allele-specific expression in admixed whole blood, with 52 ancestry-associated loci replicating. Several studies apply these resources to disease. CAS-X integrates fine-mapped eQTLs across five metabolic tissues to prioritize type 2 diabetes effector genes. PrediXSKAT weights rare coding variants by predicted cis-regulated expression to boost kernel-test power. Endometriosis GWAS cell-state prioritization proves sensitive to marker direction and donor structure. Mendelian randomization implicates midkine in pancreatic cancer.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-19"
